.TH HEARTBEAT_SENDER.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
heartbeat_sender.py \- send UDP heartbeats to a heartbeat monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B heartbeat_sender.py
.RB [ \-f | \-\-file
.IR json_file ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-name
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-s | \-\-status
.IR status ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-p | \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-i | \-\-interval
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-count
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-I | \-\-interface
.IR iface ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B heartbeat_sender.py
builds a heartbeat datagram
.RS 4
.nf
{"name": "\fIname\fR", "timestamp": "\fIUTC ISO\-8601\fR", "status": "\fIstatus\fR"}
.fi
.RE
and sends it to
.IR host : port ,
once or repeatedly.
The destination may be an IPv4 unicast, broadcast or multicast address, an
IPv6 unicast or multicast address (optionally with a
.BI % iface
scope suffix), or a host name resolved with
.BR getaddrinfo (3).
IPv6 link\-local unicast and link\-local multicast destinations require an
interface.
.PP
The wire format and its differences from the C++ sender are documented in
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIjson_file\fR
Read defaults from a JSON object with any of the keys
.BR name ,
.BR status ,
.BR host ,
.BR port ,
.BR interval ,
.BR count ,
.BR interface .
Command\-line options override file values, except that
.BR \-\-status ,
.B \-\-host
and
.B \-\-port
given with their default values do not override a different file value.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIname\fR
Sender name; the monitor's key for this sender.
Required, on the command line or in the file.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status " " \fIstatus\fR
Free\-text status string.
Default
.BR OK .
The monitor displays it but does not interpret it.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " host"
Destination.
Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIport\fR
Destination UDP port.
Default 9999.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fIseconds\fR
Send every
.I seconds
(floating point).
0, the default, sends once.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " n"
Stop after
.I n
heartbeats in interval mode.
0, the default, means unlimited.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-interface " " \fIiface\fR
Outgoing interface for IPv6 link\-local or multicast destinations.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each heartbeat as it is sent.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Heartbeat(s) sent, or interval mode stopped with Ctrl\-C.
.TP
.B 1
No name given, or the JSON file is missing or invalid.
.PP
A socket error, a host name that does not resolve, or an IPv6 link\-local
destination without an interface ends the program with a Python traceback and
status 1.
In interval mode this includes a transient error on any later send: the loop
stops at the first failure, whereas
.BR heartbeat_sender (1)
prints a warning and keeps sending.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
python3 heartbeat_sender.py \-\-name daq\-node\-01 \-\-host monitor\-host \-\-port 9999
python3 heartbeat_sender.py \-\-name runcontrol \-\-status running \-\-interval 10
python3 heartbeat_sender.py \-\-file example_sender.json
python3 heartbeat_sender.py \-\-name n1 \-\-host ff02::1%eth0
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR heartbeat_sender (1),
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
